      "knowledge": "Learners will know that: (1) the reciprocal of a real number a is 1/a, and that a × (1/a) = 1; (2) index notation expresses repeated multiplication compactly using a base and an exponent; (3) 2³ means 2 × 2 × 2 = 8 and 2¹⁰ = 1 024, so a power can be read as repeated multiplication and written in ordinary form; (4) increasing an exponent by 1 doubles the quantity when the base is 2, providing a direct link to the Kericho tea harvest context.",
