      "purposeInStoryline": "This is the opening lesson of the unit. It launches the anchoring phenomenon — a Kericho tea farmer struggling with unwieldy large-number arithmetic versus a fellow farmer who solves the same problem in two minutes using a four-figure logarithm table. Students encounter the puzzle for the first time, make their first predictions, and build the foundational language of index notation and reciprocals that every subsequent lesson will depend upon. The Driving Question Board is opened and the first student questions are posted.",
