        "teacherMoves": "Distribute group concept maps (stored since Lesson 1) and new-colour markers. Say: 'This map was started the day you first saw the tea farmer struggling with large numbers. Today you will complete it. Use the new colour so that your learning journey is visible — anyone looking at this map should see exactly when you learned each piece.' [Allow 5 minutes for map revision. Circulate and prompt:] 'Where is the connection between the Power Law and the Root Law? They are related — can you show that on the map?' / 'Where does the Kericho farm phenomenon appear on your map? It should be the centre of everything.' [After 5 minutes:] Project or hold up a photograph of the Lesson 1 concept map next to the current one. Cold-call 2 students: 'Njoroge — name one thing that changed.' / 'Chebet — if you were explaining this map to a farmer in Kericho, what would you point to first?' [Wait 8 seconds after each.] Close: 'Every node on that map is a tool. The tea farmer, the engineer at the Athi River cement plant, the epidemiologist tracking disease spread in Kisumu — they all need exactly what is on that map. You built it. You own it.'",
